otropic drugs in child and adolescent psychiatric disorders</article-title><source>Progr Neuro Psychopharmacol Biol Psychiatry</source><year>1995</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>455</fpage><lpage>465</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0278-5846(95)00026-R</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McLeod</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Pescosolido</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Takeuchi</surname><given-names>DT</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Public attitudes toward the use of psychiatric medications for children</article-title><source>J Health Soc Behav</source><year>2004</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>67</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15179907</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hatzimanolis</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Alevizos</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Attitudes and opinion of non-psychiatric physicians and a general population sample about psychotropic drugs [in Greek]</article-title><source>Psychiatry</source><year>1999</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>135</fpage><lpage>141</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organisation</collab></person-group><source>The ICD-10 Classification of Mental and Behavioural Disordres: Clinical Descriptions and Diagnostic Guidelines</source><year>1992</year><publisher-name>Geneva: WHO</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schnittker</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Misgivings of medicine? African Americans' skepticism of psychiatric medication</article-title><source>J Health Soc Behav</source><year>2003</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>506</fpage><lpage>524</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15038146</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/1519796</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Raghavan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Zima</surname><given-names>BT</given-names></name><name><surname>Andersen</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Leibowitz</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Schuster</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Landsverk</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Psychotropic medication use in a national probability sample of children in the child welfare system</article-title><source>J Child Adolesc Psychopharmacol</source><year>2005</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>106</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15741791</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1089/cap.2005.15.97</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pappaport</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Chubinsky</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The meaning of psychotropic medication for children, adolescents, and their families</article-title><source>J Am Acad Child Adolesc Psychiatry</source><year>2000</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>1198</fpage><lpage>1200</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10986818</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00004583-200009000-00021</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hack</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Chow</surname><given-names>B</given-names></nam